Our Folger Deep hydrophone picked up this unusual orca vocalization event on March 13, 2023. Identified as Bigg’s orcas (aka Transient orcas), they were heard calling for an hour and a half! This is unusual because they are typically silent to avoid alerting their prey - seals, sea lions, and other whales. To further this mystery, these Bigg’s orcas were using “aberrant” calls, a highly modified version of their typical calls. Aberrant calls are associated with socialization in resident orcas so we’re not quite sure what this means for Bigg’s orcas!

